Error [E2417]: Explicit failure domain ``ExpectedLambdaError`` is not an Error type
  --> tests/ui/lambda_interface_error_mismatch.jet:9:13
    |
  9 | fn apply(f: fn(Int) Int !ExpectedLambdaError) Int -> f(1) ?? 0
    |             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: A `!` contract may name `Err`, a Core error, a type marked `#Error`, an all-error union, or `Never`; arbitrary value types do not describe failures.
 Fix: Use a Core error, add `#Error` to a local error type, or remove the explicit error contract.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2417

Error [E0113]: This lambda should fail with `ExpectedLambdaError`, not `OtherLambdaError`
  --> tests/ui/lambda_interface_error_mismatch.jet:12:17
    |
 12 |     print(apply((n: Int) Int !OtherLambdaError -> n))
    |                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: The lambda's error type must match what's expected here
 Fix: Use `ExpectedLambdaError` here
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0113
